    <h2>What is Aikido?</h2>
    
    <p>
      <strong>Aikido</strong> is a Japanese martial art that teaches self-defense without the need 
      to harm your opponent. In our school, we emphasize:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Effective self-defense</strong> - techniques based on biomechanics, not physical strength</li>
      <li><strong>Physical development</strong> - improved fitness, flexibility, and coordination</li>
      <li><strong>Mindfulness</strong> - stress reduction, concentration, body awareness</li>
      <li><strong>Etiquette and culture</strong> - traditional Japanese approach to martial arts</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why Train at Sesshinkan Dojo?</h2>

    <div class="benefits-list">
      <div class="benefit-item">
        <h4>Traditional Aikido</h4>
        <p>We teach in the lineage of Shihan Fumio Toyoda, directly connected to Aikikai Hombu Dojo in Tokyo.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-item">
        <h4>For Everyone</h4>
        <p>You don't need to be fit or have experience. We adapt techniques to your abilities.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-item">
        <h4>Safe Training</h4>
        <p>All techniques are performed in a controlled manner. Learn ukemi (falling) from day one.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-item">
        <h4>Community</h4>
        <p>Join a group of positive people who support each other in development.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-item">
        <h4>Certified Ranks</h4>
        <p>Opportunity to test for kyu and dan ranks within an international organization.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>How to Start Aikido Training in Gdynia?</h2>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">1</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Come to Your First Class</h4>
          <p>Arrive 15 minutes early in comfortable sportswear (sweatpants, leggings, t-shirt). Keikogi (Aikido uniform) can be purchased later.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">2</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Learn the Basics</h4>
          <p>You'll learn etiquette, warm-up exercises (Aiki Taiso), and first techniques. You'll practice with an experienced aikidoka as your partner.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">3</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Continue Regularly</h4>
          <p>Minimum 2 times per week is a good start. Consistency is more important than intensity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <div class="faq-section">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>How much does Aikido training in Gdynia cost?</h4>
        <p>The first class is free. Details about membership fees and training costs are available on-site or <a href="/en/contact.html">by contacting us</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Is Aikido effective for self-defense?</h4>
        <p>Yes! Aikido teaches effective defensive techniques. In Japan, Aikido is officially taught to elite police units. Learn more about benefits <a href="/en/aikido/benefits.html">here</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Can I train at X age / with a health condition?</h4>
        <p>Aikido is accessible to people from ages 12-13 with no upper age limit. We adapt techniques to individual capabilities. Consult your doctor if you have health concerns.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Where exactly are the training sessions held?</h4>
        <p>ACS - Academic Sports Center of the Polish Naval Academy, ul. Komandora Podporucznika Jana Grudzińskiego 1, Gdynia. Well connected to Gdańsk and Sopot.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Aikido in Tricity (Gdańsk-Sopot-Gdynia)</h2>

